{"title":"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Solution_9_(Also_similar_to_Solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 9 (Also similar to Solution 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Solution_10_(Lazy_Solution/Guesstimation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 10 (Lazy Solution/Guesstimation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trapezoid\" title=\"Trapezoid\">trapezoid</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/8/08876da827a694c5cefa70caad80220eba3476ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}\\parallel\\overline{AD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/1/5112e3976e097c4f5a5722b127fda830d1f5051b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"88\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/0/7601181389c861caf6dc7f099765a8e5cd6b4ce8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 2008$\" width=\"89\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/8/9d881203486dfe72f8e189b04d3bdd1b8df2c17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A = 37^\\circ$\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/2/6f254c148c7faa925116c11c446904510f2b7188.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle D = 53^\\circ$\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Midpoint\" title=\"Midpoint\">midpoints</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />, respectively. Find the length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbcfabd65745f2b759dea1840f9a0753b2f992e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> to meet at a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/a/71a07185b3b5b2b0a75b3b3120956bcafcba938d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AED = 180 - 53 - 37 = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"237\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/e/ade36a6d8b6d97f88722facc76700d34501ddae8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(220); defaultpen(0.7+fontsize(10)); real f=100, r=1004/f; pair A=(0,0), D=(2*r, 0), N=(r,0), E=N+r*expi(74*pi/180); pair B=(126*A+125*E)/251, C=(126*D + 125*E)/251; pair[] M = intersectionpoints(N--E,B--C); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle);  draw(B--E--C,dashed); draw(M[0]--N); draw(N--E,dashed); draw(rightanglemark(D,E,A,2)); picture p = new picture;  draw(p,Circle(N,r),dashed+linewidth(0.5)); clip(p,A--D--D+(0,20)--A+(0,20)--cycle); add(p); label(&quot;\\(A\\)&quot;,A,SW); label(&quot;\\(B\\)&quot;,B,NW); label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,C,NE); label(&quot;\\(D\\)&quot;,D,SE); label(&quot;\\(E\\)&quot;,E,NE); label(&quot;\\(M\\)&quot;,M[0],SW); label(&quot;\\(N\\)&quot;,N,S); label(&quot;\\(1004\\)&quot;,(N+D)/2,S); label(&quot;\\(500\\)&quot;,(M[0]+C)/2,S); [/asy]\" width=\"368\" height=\"195\" /></center>\n<p>As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00f21509f36fd7aa475bd99e1aa3649df8e9273a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AED = 90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" />, note that the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, is the center of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumcircle\" title=\"Circumcircle\">circumcircle</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/18167d788fd698322ba516cf8bfdba2c931fa17d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AED$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />. We can do the same with the circumcircle about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97dd577dd14751b09771a1c83d880f5142b86181.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BEC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> (or we could apply the homothety to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a30c9c946a561bfb130894432aa55948d58b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ME$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5bf33c0fc6f66ddf042e950c5f4711c78f9d387.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$NE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />). It follows that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/7/dc72b66e50821ace019d1681a1f371cea7ba834a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[NE = ND = \\frac {AD}{2} = 1004, \\quad ME = MC = \\frac {BC}{2} = 500.\\]\" width=\"433\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99d2cd12a17eb6ad63d035c2e74395c4f477234c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN = NE - ME = \\boxed{504}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"211\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nFor purposes of rigor we will show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/3/9b3458aad8f841a6682e1c3f1d600a97780e8331.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E,M,N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" /> are collinear. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/13289c89c9d61ab9e820a68dcac1ae8f1cac9a09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC} \\parallel \\overline{AD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Homothecy\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Homothecy\">homothetic</a> with respect to point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> by a ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/7/7f765b6f136f5ec0628fc96920d3e760f8eed928.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BC}{AD} = \\frac{125}{251}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"38\" />. Since the homothety carries the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, to the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/3/9b3458aad8f841a6682e1c3f1d600a97780e8331.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E,M,N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Collinear\" title=\"Collinear\">collinear</a>.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/2/ed2323da960926cb22458648f561a6953f91de51.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(220); defaultpen(0.7+fontsize(10)); real f=100, r=1004/f; pair A=(0,0), D=(2*r, 0), N=(r,0), E=N+r*expi(74*pi/180); pair B=(126*A+125*E)/251, C=(126*D + 125*E)/251; pair[] M = intersectionpoints(N--E,B--C); pair F = foot(B,A,D), G=foot(C,A,D), H=foot(M[0],A,D); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle);  draw(M[0]--N); draw(B--F,dashed); draw(C--G,dashed); draw(M[0]--H,dashed); label(&quot;\\(A\\)&quot;,A,SW); label(&quot;\\(B\\)&quot;,B,NW); label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,C,NE); label(&quot;\\(D\\)&quot;,D,NE); label(&quot;\\(F\\)&quot;,F,S); label(&quot;\\(G\\)&quot;,G,SW); label(&quot;\\(M\\)&quot;,M[0],SW); label(&quot;\\(N\\)&quot;,N,S); label(&quot;\\(H\\)&quot;,H,S); label(&quot;\\(x\\)&quot;,(N+H)/2+(0,1),S); label(&quot;\\(h\\)&quot;,(B+F)/2,W); label(&quot;\\(h\\)&quot;,(C+G)/2,W); label(&quot;\\(1000\\)&quot;,(B+C)/2,NE); label(&quot;\\(504-x\\)&quot;,(G+D)/2,S); label(&quot;\\(504+x\\)&quot;,(A+F)/2,S); label(&quot;\\(h\\)&quot;,(M[0]+H)/2,(1,0)); [/asy]\" width=\"368\" height=\"115\" /></center>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/e/74eade611e8381c664c8f7cfbe97298216501d82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F,G,H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" /> be the feet of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perpendicular\" title=\"Perpendicular\">perpendiculars</a> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/4/b048ba3bb0d98674ade06a72d05e3a6f9e22c48a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B,C,M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"16\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />, respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/a/37a966a78e4907e80e4c611598c6cc7275ea3d5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = NH$\" width=\"67\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/3/65398b9b82432e5b239c0dd7fcb4aa4e97975cc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DG = 1004 - 500 - x = 504 - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"256\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/4/1449dae469f462590f175ac6aac57a1f1c5cb0c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF = 1004 - (500 - x) = 504 + x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"268\" height=\"18\" />. Also, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/c/38c0324ce455e406ab65cd1d4c01a37168a1be8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = BF = CG = HM$\" width=\"176\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>By AA~, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/9/bc95852a36a733edbcbc421250ab0fcf7ff6cda4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AFB \\sim \\triangle CGD$\" width=\"143\" height=\"13\" />, and so \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/c/cfca0da10f6f0e68a00986199ceb62c89091a2a9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{BF}{AF} = \\frac {DG}{CG} \\Longleftrightarrow \\frac{h}{504+x} = \\frac{504-x}{h} \\Longrightarrow x^2 + h^2 = 504^2.\\]\" width=\"444\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/8/ce87117cf36fca6aec5a1c6990317052a9c283b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle MHN$\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/b/ceb2b04ba95c421f7bcafc10b910a17dd17f8092.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[MN^{2} = x^2 + h^2 = 504^2,\\]\" width=\"188\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/d/98d344830c2b1cc08bd8fc17fc9f18994576fead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN = \\boxed{504}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>If you drop perpendiculars from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and call the points where they meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> respectively, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/4/da41ffb194e726211d856640ece73eaf3b26f5f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FD = x$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/7/4e7a9ff2c23cf01443816fa5af1594ea5fac095e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EA = 1008-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"121\" height=\"13\" /> , and so you can solve an equation in tangents. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/9/61903e7e1c508159b5956305369cca5f9a13cca6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{A} = 37$\" width=\"68\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/f/53faadcc42a42d5a0a49588b5780006d530ab129.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{D} = 53$\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" />, you can solve the equation [by cross-multiplication]:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4e3d14b1fbed1c723e7721fc8ebd1cff8557f1d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\tan{37}\\times (1008-x) &amp;= \\tan{53} \\times x\\\\ \\frac{(1008-x)}{x} &amp;= \\frac{\\tan{53}}{\\tan{37}} = \\frac{\\sin{53}}{\\cos{53}} \\times\\frac{\\cos{37}}{\\sin{37}}\\end{align*}\" width=\"372\" height=\"65\" />\n</p><p>However, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/6/b966b92197ccf8e3e3d9aeae6fa5cc332b1b4ff9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{90-x} = \\sin{x}$\" width=\"138\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/6/0b61eea21c195f1b57bb1539b6af737ef8e5093c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{90-x} = \\cos{x}$\" width=\"138\" height=\"12\" /> are co-functions. Applying this,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/b/9db1ac1c039e48dfddb73fe66a3b09c659ae3007.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\frac{(1008-x)}{x} &amp;= \\frac{\\sin^2{53}}{\\cos^2{53}} \\\\ x\\sin^2{53} &amp;= 1008\\cos^2{53} - x\\cos^2{53}\\\\ x(\\sin^2{53}  + \\cos^2{53}) &amp;= 1008\\cos^2{53}\\\\ x = 1008\\cos^2{53} &amp;\\Longrightarrow 1008-x = 1008\\sin^2{53} \\end{align*}\" width=\"372\" height=\"119\" />\nNow, if we can find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/0/7800cf3beb6037bab175b2e0c3ad010c666682e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1004 - (EA + 500)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"148\" height=\"18\" />, and the height of the trapezoid, we can create a right triangle and use the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbcfabd65745f2b759dea1840f9a0753b2f992e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>The leg of the right triangle along the horizontal is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/9/e39c985ea4d84642f8b97b07840bf47ef4990484.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1004 - 1008\\sin^2{53} - 500 = 504 - 1008\\sin^2{53}.\\]\" width=\"364\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Now to find the other leg of the right triangle (also the height of the trapezoid), we can simplify the following expression:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/f/8ef1c522fba6b778ccdb3659a4dc35a87b7452fe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\tan{37} \\times 1008 \\sin^2{53} = \\tan{37} \\times 1008 \\cos^2{37} = 1008\\cos{37}\\sin{37} = 504\\sin74\\end{align*}\" width=\"600\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Now we used Pythagorean Theorem and get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbcfabd65745f2b759dea1840f9a0753b2f992e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/3/c93a20457d3178c5cc4ac4ec05ec2a748adf9286.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}&amp;\\sqrt{(1008\\sin^2{53} + 500 -1004)^2 + (504\\sin{74})^2} = 504\\sqrt{1-2\\sin^2{53} + \\sin^2{74}} \\end{align*}\" width=\"591\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/5/2356687b04914426a175c0ae5e715093bf07f0eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-2\\sin^2{53} = \\cos^2{106}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"180\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/f/5cf9a10bbff85a749548c1748256ae7e203d8ded.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2{74} = \\sin^2{106}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"134\" height=\"16\" /> so now we end up with:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/27153b4a7603af0d88f682374a8bf9deddbef0dd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[504\\sqrt{\\cos^2{106} + \\sin^2{106}} =\\fbox{504}.\\]\" width=\"253\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Plot the trapezoid such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a50823c5f72141badd0123277a1512a941a4ff5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=\\left(1000\\cos 37^\\circ, 0\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"161\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/3/ba3b27a03049562f8b69e613f0b68ec76fcc43cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=\\left(0, 1000\\sin 37^\\circ\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/c/f7cffd4bb76b7cd2e3a184065ef34d166292192a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=\\left(2008\\cos 37^\\circ, 0\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"160\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/f/91f2dd46100ce66d20f68c293e65e14c7c9ba573.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=\\left(0, 2008\\sin 37^\\circ\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"160\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>The midpoints of the requested sides are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/7/1f7dc3d892fe244196d3aa3a5eea503afe5fb730.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(500\\cos 37^\\circ, 500\\sin 37^\\circ\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"185\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/6/9f6a21426b6b431667b416a6400315fbee65918d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(1004\\cos 37^\\circ, 1004\\sin 37^\\circ\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"204\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>To find the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, we simply apply the distance formula and the Pythagorean identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/5/a958fb1f7b5b87ef62ed4a2205643ef36cb3df4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"19\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/0/cd061bcabeb8693f9108ab5d56616589a090ff8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN=\\boxed{504}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Similar to solution 1; Notice that it forms a right triangle. Remembering that the median to the hypotenuse is simply half the length of the hypotenuse, we quickly see that the length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/3/153017758566e9e66b3a8bc5f062d69fc282e1db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2008}{2}-\\frac{1000}{2}=504$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"154\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Obviously, these angles are random--the only special thing about them is that they add up to 90. So we might as well let the given angles equal 45 and 45, and now the answer is trivially <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/7/b47b99edd8b63c0f040ab7bf194a4409d72e44d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{504}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />. (The trapezoid is isosceles, and you see two 45-45-90 triangles;from there you can get the answer.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the height be h. Note that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb020b748f61dbd4ea98b66e1ee8587610ccb7d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{NH} = x$\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" /> then if we draw perpendiculars like in solution 1, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/9/eb9e396244791ef731e027cf8ae1195ec8b002dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{FN} = 500 - x, \\overline{AF} = 504 + x, \\overline{HG} = 500, \\overline{GD} = 504 - x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"451\" height=\"19\" /> Note that we wish to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b19cafc419680199d0b33235002e18192d174f23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{MN} = \\sqrt{x^2 + h^2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" /> Let's find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70427929f9986b69044c74db9ba74b4075abcaf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(53)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> in two ways. Finding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70427929f9986b69044c74db9ba74b4075abcaf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(53)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cb98cceed7bd43e503254097c1e06aaf025e880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BAF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/a/70a967a97fa56900b6f72135094b76210342bba7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(53) = \\frac{504+x}{h}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"154\" height=\"38\" /> Finding it from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/0/cf0d3ae2af38718f27f122c77afc6e42735c51a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CDG$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/5/c65ba86eb6abb235ec2911ba684361b7b57e8be7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{h}{504-x}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"67\" height=\"38\" /> Setting these equal yields \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/9/899d64b8f1f45880f4df817b4a65f4b09eba2284.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{504+x}{h}=\\frac{h}{504-x} \\rightarrow h^2 = 504^2-x^2 \\rightarrow \\sqrt{x^2+h^2} = \\sqrt{504^2} = \\boxed{504}\\]\" width=\"526\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8\">Solution 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rotate trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/0/7f0b91fbd521ba4ac82d2e1d834873ec29258866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MNCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"14\" /> 180 degrees around point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/a/9aafc7e3cc1eafce5e16d3a45250eeda7b1a6526.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AN$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> coincides with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/7/7778098e6f10ecdaf5eb74e56dcbfe099f22e785.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ND$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" />. Let the image of trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/0/7f0b91fbd521ba4ac82d2e1d834873ec29258866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MNCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/f/e3f151b98f2c5aeaddefd53d5862fe5fe13d8ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ANM&#39;C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />. Since angles are preserved during rotations, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/6/8866d39053df91c216af4a7566f5eecc567f0374.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC&#39; = 37^{\\circ} + 53 ^{\\circ} =90 ^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"210\" height=\"17\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/5/895ed537d57be5984124921f66e8f5ff79824f39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM=CM=C&#39;M&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"162\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/a/2baa2a1c19c1b0f89121604e6871d74c29921572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM || C&#39;M&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/a/2ba405f279c33ea817cf0875d9589dfe76c29845.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BMM&#39;C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> is a parallelogram. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/904a35402a3fe45b102ceef6a200b68f52f1c776.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MM&#39;=BC&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"104\" height=\"16\" />.\nLet the point where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/c/5bc856e7f29652b2c928f2c025ed9befbab1873e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC&#39;$\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec846ebd51dfaa2a48ffd779205a3e6ceb706063.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BMNE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"14\" /> is a parallelogram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/5/3a503b37141a27aabbdddf821c69edebee90ed13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=AN-BM=1004-500-504$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"301\" height=\"16\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/6/4e68f33d25e88f8170426229710e63376ea4875f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=EC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/d/43d7ccea57bbda805f6f7b0703bcdfc47ee05955.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC= 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> is a median to the hypotenuse of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/3/4539f6216a0d7943157be08d304af077df7ece7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BAC&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/4/5149e4ed6de30116ea52634cca3530bc60e2cc1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC&#39;=2 AE= 1008$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"158\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/7/837733930639c95dceaecd79c244f457596f4d66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=MN=\\boxed{504}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"159\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_9_.28Also_similar_to_Solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_9_(Also_similar_to_Solution_1)\">Solution 9 (Also similar to Solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 9 (Also similar to Solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Draw line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a30c9c946a561bfb130894432aa55948d58b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ME$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> from point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> that intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Draw <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/1/551fab3023436463570c8159f37571740d523aa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MF$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> from point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66492998689e8303534c9e4f3ba1fa650fd41f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> that intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Note that triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/c/4ac1d461416c45893687ed0aa94a8ce431457594.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EMF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> is a right triangle because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/f/54f6239b4b68d33eb63386fb0e204f8e84c23213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC&#39; = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"16\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/b/62b1e34c849cc63fb02af6040868b86ba9a15020.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EN$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f19a44636c5b550d5ce104f314a328897ea4aab0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DN - CM = 1004 - 500 = 504$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"252\" height=\"16\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/5/6058bb5d4e2985b8bfad7312d392af95b7d1e372.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CDEM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" /> is a parallelogram. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/3/7030131c3d4c89168cc5701e2be82799c792025e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FN$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/8/968cbf6d242b880f021a38694eac3850911eba18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AN - BM = 504$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"140\" height=\"16\" /> so N is the midpoint of the hypotenuse of right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/c/4ac1d461416c45893687ed0aa94a8ce431457594.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EMF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />. The midpoint of the hypotenuse in a right triangle is equidistant from all three vertices, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/d/98d344830c2b1cc08bd8fc17fc9f18994576fead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN = \\boxed{504}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_10_.28Lazy_Solution.2FGuesstimation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_10_(Lazy_Solution/Guesstimation)\">Solution 10 (Lazy Solution/Guesstimation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 10 (Lazy Solution/Guesstimation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Drop perpendiculars on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>You can see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/f/6df270e02069aaa2009f745d393b158855c8ba2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY = 2008-1000 = 1008$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"213\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/3/fe3134e7632702ae8999860535f87b600adfe4db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YD = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/3/61329432d5926945405b9848cc6c32fc64135833.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN = BX = CY = h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"181\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/b/f6b9f4995c3818b4b9fc003b8daf18c89a2628ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX = 1008 - a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"124\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>We will also get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/3/c63fe7927cb0f112fe678a1e3ecaf6d074e3d60e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YCD = XAB = 37°$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"158\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Observe that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/2/0129048fe7f30325694318b33216fabcdd82caaa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan 37^\\circ = \\frac{h}{1008-a} = \\frac{a}{h}\\]\" width=\"188\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Solving for h:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/c/aac4aac2d963e35be7bf89a54b9fd508f7fe686c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[h = \\sqrt{(a)(1008-a)}\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>To obtain h from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f6f99f126bd33f60bd80f63787d0b42d64ee850.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq h \\leq 999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"17\" />, only possible natural value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/f/87f385769245cc3c249ec34e15661c168bfb48e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$504$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/c/4cc7aadb9702fe548c2bdc74dd1e948732706d3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1008-a) = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdbc74323a5e8a4c1523597d0795a7198828e088.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{h = 504}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"75\" height=\"26\" />\n</p><p>Note: You can also complete the square in the above equation and then see that the only solution is 504.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II\" title=\"2008 AIME II\">2008 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2008\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://usamts.org/Solutions/Solution2_2_18.pdf\">USAMTS Year 18 Problem 2</a></li></ul>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017214501\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.083 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.105 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 869/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1806/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 29194/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.527      1 -total\n 59.52%    8.646      1 Template:AIME_box\n 37.90%    5.506      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6668:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017214501 and revision id 291004. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}